hi the polls tell us that Americans do  not want the Supreme Court overturn its  1973 roe v wade ruling on abortion in a  Gallup question from July 64% did not  want the decision overturned new polls  from Fox News and the Kaiser Family  Foundation produced similar results that  said most Americans believe that  abortion should be legal only under  certain circumstances and they are  willing to put considerable restrictions  on the procedure in gálvez polling on  the issue for example around 60 percent  say it should be possible for a woman to  obtain a legal abortion in the first  three months of a pregnancy that dropped  sharply to around 30 percent when people  are asked about abortions in the second  trimester and only 10% when pollsters  ask about the third trimester in gallops  latest poll for May this year 48% of  people said that they considered  themselves to be pro-life and an  identical 48 percent said that they were  pro-choice the split reflects Americans  beliefs in the sanctity of life  and the importance of individual choice  do you think Rovio age should be  overturned let us know in your comments  also let us know what other topics you'd  like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds  and be sure to LIKE and subscribe for  more research and videos from AEI
 

